# =============================================================================
# .env — committed defaults for the digital-matrix blog
# =============================================================================
# This file is checked into git. Local-only overrides go in .env.local
# (gitignored). Vercel-prod overrides go in the Vercel project settings UI.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed `VITE_` to client-side code. Anything
# else stays server-side at build time. Never put secrets here — this file
# ships in the public repo.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_MOTION_OVERRIDE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Forces the device-tier motion policy to a fixed state for every visitor.
# Layered config — see src/lib/motion-config.ts for the full precedence chain.
#
# Values:
#   on    — animations forced ON regardless of tier (mobile/tablet animate too)
#   off   — animations forced OFF regardless of tier (desktop is static too)
#   <unset> — honour tier defaults (desktop=on, mobile/tablet=off). Default.
#
# A per-browser localStorage value of "on" or "off" wins over this setting.
# See src/lib/motion-config.ts for usage.
#
# Uncomment the line below to flip the build-time default:
# VITE_MOTION_OVERRIDE=on
